   "meta": {
    "application": "BambuStudio-02.05.00.66",
    "profile_title": "Extend game across multiple boards",
    "profile_notes": "I am a big fan of the creativeness and possibilities of this game that Applepie created, and many others have shared print profiles on. I thought you could simulate robbers tunneling from the basement of the building next store by combining two boards. Lots of variations: Multiple players on the left try and rob the vault on the right Three players on each side try and rob the vault on the opposite side Three players on one side try and rob two vaults on the opposite side… Lot's more that others can contribute! This print configuration lists the additional components needed to combine two boards. You will need to print out double the components of the main game, plus the items in this print profile. This profile contains: Larger storage box Attachment brackets to store one board below and one board above the storage box A “tunnel” piece that is a bracket that holds the boards together A special gear that transfers movement from one board to the other “through the tunnel” The connecting gear is placed on the middle position of one of the player aids, the assembly is then placed in between two boards. The tunnel bracket holds the two boards relative to each other and against the middle transfer gear. The expanded storage contains room for: Double components Print in place containers to hold Gears 1-4 Stacking trays to hold the double quantity of Player Aids and Gears 5-6 Secure locations for Two vaults with @3Dja's magnetic vault doors and two of his awesome “Jails” Print in place container to hold Axl_print3D's (@axloury) beautiful dice Many thanks to Applepie, 3Dja, and Axl_print3D (axloury).",
    "creation_date": "2026-03-02",
    "slicer": "Bambu Studio",
    "printer": "Bambu Lab X1 Carbon",
