   "meta": {
    "application": "BambuStudio-01.10.01.50",
    "profile_title": "Storage Case for Extended Vault/Magnetic Door - with Insert",
    "profile_notes": ".4mm nozzle, 2mm layer, minimal support with support blocker modifier and painted non-support. I finally got around to modifying Applepie's storage case to fit the vault extension/magnetic vault cover that I posted a couple weeks ago. Everything in this case is exactly the same as the original designer's except a longer compartment to allow the extended vault to fit and I also added an insert module that holds the coins, thieves, and die (up to 16mm). The insert has a lower storage compartment that has a jail for the thief player pieces (will hold up to 6 so you can have a couple of additional player colors from the designer's profile). The jail has a gate that safely locks the little criminals away! If 4 optional magnets are used, it will have 2 positions, minimum security and maximum security! The top part of the insert has a compartment that stores the game coins (regular and expanded amount) and it will also hold a die up to 16mm. The coin compartment has a slidable cover to keep these little suckers from bouncing around, can't be risking losing gold coins with the state of the economy and all! The insert assembly has pockets for 3 x 2 disk magnets in the insert body and the gate that are optional - it works a lot cooler with the magnets, but the thieves will be unable to escape even if you decide to forego the magnets. Double check magnet polarity before pressing in, should be able to install them without glue. The lower section of the insert has minimal support - for the 2 slots on the side and the for the roof of the jail cell. Be sure to remove any straggling support material form the cell area so the little fellas don't get hung up when being locked away! Thanks again to Applepie for sharing this phenomenal model!",
