    "profile_notes": "A two-piece print profile for the main board. In printing the main board upside down, a smoother playing surface is achieved when using a high-temperature, non-textured plate. Making the board a two-piece reduces the printing time to seven and a half hours, versus printing the one-piece board upside down, which had more than an 11 hour print time, and had a lot of support material to remove. The upside down one-piece board also resulted in a rough surface of mating geometry that contacts the input gear and pawl components. Once the two pieces are printed out, the flange can be attached to the board by super glue. Assembly proceeds normally from there. Added logo to the reverse side of the main board.",
